# SFT execution status v0.130: corrected generated native coordinator passed

2026-09-28. **The corrected v3 generated-only coordinator passed its one-shot
native Linux run.** The output-parent correction now has native success
evidence, not only local tests. Gate 5 is still incomplete: this tiny fixture
is not real 4B import, full-size host admission, training authorization or
production eligibility. No S3 model/dataset access, GPU, inference or training.

## Concrete result

The approved v0.3 attempt resumed after AWS login. Exact resource lookup
confirmed no VM had previously been created for its client token. Existing
temporary network/key resources were reused; no replacement instance or retry.
Source archive v0.4 and all prepared artifact bindings matched before launch.

The single t3.large instance used Ubuntu 24.04, Python 3.12.3 and systemd 255;
encrypted 20-GiB gp3 delete-on-termination storage, standard CPU credits, no IAM
profile, mandatory IMDS tokens, pinned SSH host key and endpoint-only SSH ingress.
Boot health, expiry, worker identity, cgroups and HTTPS setup quota were checked
before staging. All 34 CPU wheel hashes passed. Setup accounted 290,428,454
inbound HTTPS bytes under the 1-GiB non-resetting quota, with zero drops.

The supervisor returned exit 0 and `passed_generated_only`:

- Actual tiny generated checkpoint conversion and packaging completed.
- Both full input audits completed; independent package checksum consumer passed.
- 59 staged source/input files remained unchanged. Separately, all 49 original
  staged release source hashes matched after the run.
- Coordinator content reservations: 13,360,175 read bytes and 1,575,578 private
  write bytes. These are cooperative content counters, not exhaustive physical
  I/O accounting or a cumulative native-write quota.
- Both exact cgroups were absent, generated tmpfs was unmounted and empty,
  and neither failure nor cleanup-failure records existed.
- Native aggregate result was copied byte-for-byte locally and its SHA-256
  matched the remote record:
  `bf0988e911592777972d31260e9e55a2f2d89482ef313dbcc156f18d2bed2676`.

Independent polling observed preparation's successful exit-zero terminal
snapshot. It missed import's short-lived terminal snapshot; that field remains
null. A separate bounded exact-unit journal check confirmed successful
deactivation for both units, and independently confirmed their cgroups absent.
The supervisor itself validated both terminal outcomes before accepting success.
No missing snapshot has been invented. Sampled memory maxima were 284,286,976
bytes for preparation and 283,357,184 for import, not exhaustive peak claims.

## Preserved bounds and closure

Each worker retained 2-GiB RAM, zero swap, 64 tasks and 90-second limits;
controller/outer limits remained 240/300 seconds. Two 64-MiB tmpfs capacities
were retained. Network/GPU isolation, read-only inputs and source, frozen
coordinator gates, exclusive attempt/no-retry behavior and raw-text suppression
were not relaxed. Old failed evidence and source bundles remain unchanged.

Instance `i-05307b74511bb96dd` launched at 06:09:59 UTC and was confirmed
terminated before cleanup completion at 06:17:08 UTC. Volume
`vol-0bb6ac61268b70cf1` was confirmed absent. Endpoint
`eice-0241799050f9654fd` reached delete-complete. Groups
`sg-0f89fb45df38a1f16` and `sg-0f48d6278977b777d`, and key registration
`key-0c8bce94442ee344a`, returned successful deletion. Only this attempt's
resources were changed. Actual invoice cost is not claimed.

Generated VM data was ephemeral and is not recoverable. Private aggregate
authorization/resource/result/cleanup records remain in
`artifacts/lumi-vm-coordinator-native-attempt-v0.3/`. No commit or push occurred.

## Roadmap boundary and next necessary step

The generated native coordinator qualification blocker is closed for this
exact source/runtime/host-control combination. This does **not** establish
full-size memory/disk/read budgets or authorize removing generated-only scope.
The old cumulative-native-write route remains closed.

Next: prepare the real-input host-bound entry/admission using the preserved
S3 checkpoint lineage and explicit full-size resource/rights constraints, then
obtain the required bounded execution approval and perform the actual CPU
import plus independent package verification. The consumed tiny-check approval
cannot be reused for acquisition or real import. Gate 6 GPU smoke/save/resume
and SFT, Gate 7 evaluation, and Gate 8 serving remain later.
